## **Proposed Sprint Breakdown for Agent Implementation**

I recommend **8 two-week sprints** organized by vertical slices that deliver end-to-end functionality:

### **Sprint 0: Foundation & Infrastructure (2 weeks)**
**Goal:** Get the entire stack running with basic scaffolding
- ✅ Create Docker Compose configuration (9 services + 2 networks + 5 volumes)
- ✅ Set up PostgreSQL with pgcrypto extension
- ✅ Create Alembic migration structure for all 9 schemas (34 tables)
- ✅ Build `init.sh` automated setup script
- ✅ Configure .env.example with all 30+ environment variables
- ✅ Verify all services start and communicate
- **Deliverable:** `docker compose up` brings up healthy stack

### **Sprint 1: Auth & Profile Management (2 weeks)**
**Goal:** Users can register, login, and manage household profiles
- ✅ Implement auth schema (users, sessions, households)
- ✅ Build FastAPI auth router (login, logout, JWT validation)
- ✅ Implement identity schema (profiles, profile_fields with versioning)
- ✅ Build profiles API (CRUD + pause/unpause)
- ✅ Create React auth flow (login, logout, protected routes)
- ✅ Build profile management UI with field versioning
- ✅ Write unit tests for auth + profile logic
- **Deliverable:** Admin can create profiles and manage PII fields

### **Sprint 2: Broker Registry & Discovery (2 weeks)**
**Goal:** System can discover and manage data broker registry
- ✅ Implement registry schema (brokers, broker_playbooks, playbook_versions)
- ✅ Build brokers API router (list, search, playbook upload/activation)
- ✅ Create n8n workflows (5 workflows for broker discovery)
- ✅ Implement HMAC-signed webhook endpoint
- ✅ Build broker registry UI (browse, search, manual overrides)
- ✅ Seed initial broker dataset
- ✅ Write integration tests for webhook upsert flow
- **Deliverable:** n8n can auto-discover brokers and populate registry

### **Sprint 3: Playwright Automation Engine (2 weeks)**
**Goal:** Headless browser can execute playbooks
- ✅ Build Playwright microservice (FastAPI on :8001)
- ✅ Implement browser context pool management
- ✅ Create all 16 action handlers (navigate, fill, click, extract, etc.)
- ✅ Build token resolution system (16 interpolation values)
- ✅ Implement confirmation detection (text + URL patterns)
- ✅ Add screenshot capture and structured storage
- ✅ Create CAPTCHA detection and manual escalation
- ✅ Build fake Playwright service for testing
- ✅ Write unit tests for action handlers and token resolver
- **Deliverable:** Playwright service can execute playbook JSON against test broker

### **Sprint 4: Scanning Workflow (2 weeks)**
